  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Pages are translucent envelopes, open at the top edge, printed with text and images in black.  Each envelope holds a card with text and illustrations in colors. The reader is invited to remove and rearrange the cards to create his or her own story.  Illustrated leaves with tabs divide the nine sections.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Bound in purple cloth over boards with orange spine, and sewn with exposed green thread.  A window in the upper board reveals the title.  Issued in slipcase.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"Card images screen printed by Thomas Wojak at the W.O.R.K.S. in San Francisco.  All other parts of this book were letterpress printed at Flying Fish Press by Julie Chen"--Colophon.</subfield>
